CYBERVS DOMINATVS X LISTENING STATION
by GhostExodus

CYBERVS DOMINATVS X LISTENING STATION is a Windows desktop OSINT application designed to monitor selected X accounts, preserve findings locally, search collected material, document investigative observations, and gradually build a larger archive over time.

It operates through an authenticated X browser session rather than requiring the investigator to paste browser cookies directly into the application.

1. Target-account monitoring

You can add X usernames as monitored sources.

For each source, the application can collect and organize:

Original posts
Replies written by the monitored account
Reposts or retweets
Comments and replies made by other users
Visible timestamps
Post URLs
Engagement information displayed by X
Media references where available

Each monitored account becomes a searchable source inside the application.

2. Live Feed

The Live Feed displays content collected from the accounts you are monitoring.

You can filter the feed using checkboxes, allowing you to show or hide:

Posts
Replies
Reposts
Third-party comments

You can also select an individual source to view only that account’s collected activity.

The local feed is separate from the live X website. It is a preserved investigative dataset built from completed collection sweeps.

3. Open the real post or thread

Every captured post, reply, repost or comment can be opened directly on X.

The Open Real Thread function launches the actual post inside the application’s authenticated X browser session.

This allows you to:

Read the complete conversation
Review surrounding replies
See newer engagement
Confirm the current state of the post
Compare the live thread with the locally preserved record

This is useful because a local finding may remain in the database even if the live post is later changed, deleted or restricted.

4. Keyword searching

The application can search across the content it has collected.

Searches can cover:

Post text
Replies
Reposts
Comments
Usernames
Display names
Investigative notes

This allows you to identify references to names, organizations, locations, phrases, hashtags, events or other investigative terms.

The application searches the local archive, so previously collected material remains searchable without repeatedly loading the same pages from X.

5. Search presets

Reusable search presets can be created for recurring investigative topics.

A preset can contain:

One or more keywords
Exact phrases
Search terms associated with a case
Selected monitored accounts
Content-type restrictions

Presets can use matching behavior such as:

Match any term
Match all terms

This makes it possible to repeatedly run the same investigative query without rebuilding it every time.

Example preset:

Terms:
"fundraiser"
"donation"
"crypto"
"wallet"

Sources:
Selected monitored accounts

Mode:
Match any term
6. Investigative notes

Analyst notes can be attached directly to individual findings.

A note can document:

Why the post is relevant
Connections to another person or account
Identity assessments
Timeline observations
Unverified hypotheses
Follow-up actions
Evidentiary concerns
Links to external research

Notes can be edited or deleted later.

There is also a dedicated Analyst Notes workspace where notes can be reviewed and searched across the investigation.

This keeps the investigator’s interpretation separate from the original captured content.

7. Followers and following extraction

The application can collect accounts appearing in a target’s:

Followers list
Following list

For each visible account, it can retain information such as:

Username
Display name
Biography text
Profile image reference
Profile URL
Which monitored account the relationship came from
Whether the account was a follower or followed account

The application can extract either list separately or run both.

